      "claim": "L4/L5 Caco-2 records show mannitol has very low apparent permeability (e.g., Papp 0.18-0.48 x 10^-6 cm/s) and no net efflux (ER ~1.0; C59, C62, C65, C68, C69), yet mannitol still reaches about 20% human F; therefore low Caco-2 permeability and absence of efflux are not affirmative evidence for F < 20% in small polar molecules.",
      "card_ids": ["C59", "C62", "C65", "C68", "C69", "C01", "C06"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No L5 record provides direct gut-wall efflux or intestinal metabolism data for ascorbic acid; the relevant mannitol mechanistic records show no efflux/transporter involvement, and the query prior notes possible active transport as an enhancer.",
      "card_ids": ["C59", "C62", "C68", "C69"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
