    "Dose dependence and saturation of ascorbic acid absorption are not captured.",
    "Transfer from mannitol/glucose/sorbitol/propylene glycol contexts is qualitative; species, doses, and patient status differ."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%): human F estimates for mannitol (~20%), glucose (0.72-0.84), sorbitol (0.36-0.38), and propylene glycol (very high) support that small polar polyhydroxy compounds can meet the threshold; L3 mannitol exposure is dose-linear; L4/L5 Caco-2 records show mannitol has low permeability and no efflux yet still reaches about 20% human F, so low permeability/absence of efflux is not affirmative low-F evidence. No direct ascorbic acid low-F or gut-wall efflux/metabolism record is present; the query prior notes possible active transport. Prediction remains high with moderate confidence."
}

